docs/MORIARTY-BACKEND-REQUIREMENTS.md:39:| ZR03, ZR06, ZR07, ZR11 | ZKIR semantics/constraints, compiler and ledger context binding | Prove source/intent/effect correspondence and mandatory-predicate enforcement; U1/U2/U4 |
docs/MORIARTY-BACKEND-REQUIREMENTS.md:41:| ZR10 | Ledger current-state/consumption interfaces plus application contracts | Head/absence checks and unique single-lineage consumption at U2; completeness/concurrency/composition extensions at U3/U4 |
docs/MORIARTY-BACKEND-REQUIREMENTS.md:42:| ZR12, ZR13 | ZKIR, prover/verifier resource interfaces and ledger costing | Bind per-stage/cumulative work and reserves; U1/U3/U4 |
docs/MORIARTY-CONSOLIDATED-DESIGN.md:52:Assets and domain-qualified quantities have exact identities and units. Checked finite-width arithmetic, overflow, rounding and prices are explicit. U0 freezes canonical price orientation, unit dimensions, per-primitive rounding direction and beneficiary policy in the numeric profile; U1 certificates bind that profile. Amounts must not silently become field elements modulo the proof field. DeFiFormal prices are quote-per-base while the current Moriarty convention is base-per-quote: adaptation requires an explicit dimensioned conversion and directed rounding, not a rename.
docs/MORIARTY-PRODUCT-CONTRACT.md:11:The [consolidated vision and design](MORIARTY-CONSOLIDATED-DESIGN.md), [single U0–U7 roadmap](../ROADMAP.md), and [next ZKIR/recursion requirements](MORIARTY-BACKEND-REQUIREMENTS.md) integrate the research agenda. P/C/K identifiers remain requirement lineage; they are not independent delivery queues. The user supplied a planning assumption on 2026-09-19 that comprehensive Midnight recursion arrives in about six months. Plan full native recursive compliance and private multi-parent composition accordingly; current interface limitations do not remove that scope. The timing is not a verified release claim.
README.md:62:Amounts need asset identities, units and domains. Prices need a declared orientation. Fees, rounding and overflow need exact rules. Settlement bindings must specify how nominal obligations convert into ledger asset quantities. Otherwise, a perfectly valid proof may establish arithmetic over values whose financial interpretation was wrong at the outset. Moriarty's design therefore treats these choices as part of the semantic contract carried into compilation and verification.
ROADMAP.md:15:The user supplied a six-month planning assumption on 2026-09-19: comprehensive Midnight recursion around March 2027. Full native recursion and private multi-parent composition are target capabilities, not optional replacements. Prepare U4 and the [next ZKIR/recursion requirements](docs/MORIARTY-BACKEND-REQUIREMENTS.md) during U0/U1. U1 will determine whether currently released interfaces support an early scoped milestone; their limitations do not reduce MC03/MC06. Revalidate actual released interfaces and costs before claiming support.
ROADMAP.md:21:| U0 | One semantic contract and current target matrix | None | Versioned source/Core embeddings; stage, intent, effect, authority, history and failure judgments; canonical price orientation, unit dimensions, per-primitive rounding direction and beneficiary policy in the numeric profile; K-reference reconciliation status; actual compiler/ZKIRv3/verifier/key/ledger pins; field-by-field enforcement map; explicit trust and unresolved interface premises |
ROADMAP.md:22:| U1 | Certified minimum basis and native feasibility | U0 | Native certificate for the first exact arithmetic primitive and every primitive needed by the initial slice; valid-witness completeness and adversarial-witness soundness; caller preconditions and declared logical/target cost relation; measured signature/phase/recursive-certificate feasibility with retained bytes and limits. Failed or unavailable interfaces remain blocked, not certified |
ROADMAP.md:23:| U2 | General supported single-stage source-to-Midnight path | U0; required U1 slice basis | Newly authored program plus a structurally contrasting program, canonical signed intention, actual pinned ZKIRv3, native verification and complete effect readback; scope-qualified contract/refinement/transition/history enforcement, replay and signed failure controls. Generality argument covers the admitted grammar. Existing loan/swap requirements remain |
ROADMAP.md:24:| U3 | Conditional settlement, partial progress and recovery | U2 | Two-asset programmable escrow, recipient/document conditions, partial fill, persistent duty and continuation, joins, late-success/refund race, separate recovery authority, reserved work and state-cap boundary; actual phase effects and objective hostile controls |
ROADMAP.md:25:| U4 | Native history and private composition | U2; U3 lifecycle invariants; accepted SP07/SP08 semantic inputs for each claimed successor scope | Retained two-step native recursive financial evidence, legitimate genesis and bounded multi-parent compatibility; separate-party private handoff and every retained composition operator demonstrated without the federated kernel; authenticated completeness, unique consumption, disclosure and witness-availability evidence. Ledger induction alone does not close MC03/MC06 |
ROADMAP.md:27:| U6 | Composable financial libraries and full conformance | U2; applicable U3/U4/U5 interfaces per family | All retained ACTUS fixtures/fields, DeFi action rows and held-out behaviors; independent source expectations; separate semantic/native/local/Preview coverage; exact arithmetic/rounding, gross economics and persistent duties. Source preparation may start earlier; no skipped family counts as complete |
ROADMAP.md:28:| U7 | Independent developer release | U2–U6 and all retained release predicates | Clean public installation, independently authored non-fixture program and own-wallet submission, two-builder reproducibility, objective negative controls, complete MC/SP/G evidence, pilots/baselines/licenses/privacy obligations and honest scope statement |
ROADMAP.md:30:Acceptance dependencies are not a ban on independent preparation. U0 and U1 investigate recursive feasibility early; U4 owns its full acceptance evidence. Conditional reference examples and library source analysis can inform U0. Keep one delivery implementation slice active; independent review and bounded feasibility can proceed alongside it. No new planner, campaign framework or parallel application-specific compiler is needed.
ROADMAP.md:32:Financial semantic preparation from SP07/SP08 can begin during U0 and must be accepted before full SP09 mandatory acceptance for that successor scope. U4 can qualify an explicitly bounded subset earlier, but this is not full SP09 or full supported-language MC05. U6 owns later financial extensions and must requalify affected source/Core, native, consumption and mandatory-acceptance predicates; full closure waits for those accepted inputs and requalification. This is an artifact dependency, not a cycle requiring all U6 conformance before any U4 work.
ROADMAP.md:34:U2 may deliver a scoped ledger-induced history profile while U4 is unresolved. It must label that scope and cannot declare full MC05, MC03, MC06 or full-agenda release complete. An unavailable native interface blocks its dependent claims, not correct independent source research.
ROADMAP.md:38:Finish U0's current-target and semantic integration matrix, then connect the smallest useful signed financial stage through U1/U2. The next extended discriminator is U3: spend at most 11 A including at most 1 A fees to receive at least 20 B on successful completion, with exact recipients, domains, permitted partial outcomes and recovery. Two independently produced candidates may supply different authorized routes through direct local/manual authoring or standalone tools; this checks objective route neutrality without U5 infrastructure. U3 needs no federation. U5 separately qualifies live coordinated solver services on the same program. Recipient acceptance and an authenticated document predicate guard delivery; a committed partial stage retains its obligation.
ROADMAP.md:46:Obligation and trust reports accompany U0–U2. Exact advisory refinement checking follows a supported encoding and evaluator-replayed counterexamples. Typed holes and bounded synthesis follow demonstrated usefulness; they are optional for manual authorship. All generated candidates pass the same objective pipeline and preserve every applicable signed constraint.

