    48	
    49	## Evaluation and publication
    50	
    51	`/5` type-checks every action, selects one action, admits owned lifecycle
    52	input, validates snapshots, executes the prefix once, prepares the lifecycle
    53	kernel once, then executes the entire `ensures` suffix once. Financial PRE
    54	never changes within one source action. Same-call Originate followed by
    55	Accrue is permitted as explicit ordered descriptors. Accrue target
    56	denomination is checked against the agreement binding even though Accrue
    57	has no nominal operand.
    58	
    59	Work is prefix reductions plus kernel actions plus suffix reductions.
    60	Failed suffix after a tentative financial event publishes no state, effects
    61	or IDs. Canonical compact financial post must be <=65536 bytes and fully
    62	re-admissible after kernel debit and after suffix debit.
    63	
    64	This slice does not execute K, construct a proof, or submit a public
    65	transaction.

